RuyaOS patch for xwayland-satellite (RUY-434, ADR-034). Written against 0.8.3.

What: bind xdg_wm_base at the version the compositor offers, from 1 up to 6
(upstream asks for 2..=6), and name that version in the existing warning.

Why: ruya-shell's compositor is QtWaylandCompositor, whose XdgShell offers
xdg_wm_base version 1 (hard-coded in qtwayland, still so on its dev branch).
Unpatched, the satellite panics at start with "Could not bind xdg_wm_base:
UnsupportedVersion" (RUY-1, Dell). Version 2 only adds the tiled toplevel
states; the requests of version 3 (popup reposition) stay behind the existing
"version < 3" checks, so version 1 needs no other change.

Upstream state: not offered upstream (owner decision). Drop this patch once
qtwayland offers xdg_wm_base >= 2; it is harmless until then.

--- a/src/server/mod.rs
+++ b/src/server/mod.rs
@@ -509,12 +509,13 @@
         let qh = queue.handle();

         let xdg_wm_base = global_list
-            .bind::<XdgWmBase, _, _>(&qh, 2..=6, ())
+            .bind::<XdgWmBase, _, _>(&qh, 1..=6, ())
             .expect("Could not bind xdg_wm_base");

         if xdg_wm_base.version() < 3 {
             warn!(
-                "xdg_wm_base version 2 detected. Popup repositioning will not work, and some popups may not work correctly."
+                "xdg_wm_base version {} detected. Popup repositioning will not work, and some popups may not work correctly.",
+                xdg_wm_base.version()
             );
         }

